UPDATE companies SET description='Established in 1989 in Morgan City, Louisiana, LAPCO Manufacturing, Inc. has spent over three decades producing flame-resistant workwear for industrial workers.

LAPCO manufactures a range of FR garments including coveralls, jackets, shirts, bib overalls, jeans, and outerwear. Products are made from fabrics such as 100% cotton, 88/12 cotton-nylon blends, 95/5 cotton-spandex knits, and 13-ounce cotton denim, with weights from 6 to 13 ounces. The company also offers a women''s FR line and performance outerwear designed for cold-weather conditions. Custom coverall orders are a noted part of the business, with the company emphasizing quick turnaround.

Primary customers work in oil and gas, electric utility, refining, and petrochemical sectors. LAPCO sells through a distributor network and directly to end users via its website. Testimonials from pipeline workers and safety professionals highlight the brand''s use in daily field operations. The company also provides FR education resources and guides for safety program managers.

LAPCO positions itself on service, promoting ''Built on Service'' as a core differentiator. Distributors cite pain-free inventory acquisition and responsive support, while end users note the company''s willingness to listen to challenges and adapt designs. The stated purpose centers on safety, reliability, and modern styling that workers want to wear.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flame-resistant garment manufacturing", "Custom coverall production", "Distributor supply chain support", "FR safety education and resources"], "industries": ["Oil and gas", "Electric utility", "Refining", "Petrochemical"], "materials": ["100% Cotton", "88/12 Blend", "95/5 Cotton Spandex Blend", "13oz. 100% Cotton Denim", "6oz. Inherent Knit", "7oz. 100% Cotton", "7oz. 88/12 Blend"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fast turnaround on custom coverall orders", "Distributor-focused service with pain-free inventory acquisition", "Responsive customer support that adapts to client challenges", "Quality FR garments compliant with arc flash and flash fire standards", "Modern, comfortable designs for workforce acceptance"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 -> db", "Headquarters at 98 Glenwood Street, Morgan City, LA 70380 -> /", "Industries served: oil and gas, electric utility, refining, petrochemical -> / and db", "Product lines: FR coveralls, jackets, shirts, bib overalls, jeans, outerwear -> /", "Materials: 100% Cotton, 88/12 Blend, 95/5 Cotton Spandex Blend, 13oz Cotton Denim, 6oz Inherent Knit -> /", "Custom coverall orders with fast turnaround -> / (testimonial)", "Distributor program with customer service and inventory acquisition -> / (Built on Service section)", "FR education guides and industry resources -> /", "Social media presence: Twitter, Facebook, Pinterest, Instagram, YouTube -> /", "Company name indicates manufacturing -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Workers in the oil and gas, electric utility, refining, and petrochemical industries have utilized LAPCO Premium Workwear products since 1989.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lapco-manufacturing-inc-headquarters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LEDtronics was founded in 1983 in Torrance, California, as an American manufacturer of LED lighting and indicator products. The company has operated from its Southern California base for over four decades, producing LED bulbs, panel indicators, and lighting assemblies domestically.

The product line spans miniature and intermediate based LEDs, relampable and non-relampable panel indicators, PC board LEDs, discrete and surface-mount devices, as well as indoor and outdoor lighting fixtures. LEDtronics focuses on direct LED replacements for incandescent miniature lamps and indicators, serving both standard and custom requirements.

Customers come from industrial controls, defense and aerospace, power plants and utilities, transportation and railroad, cities and municipalities, elevators and escalators, commercial offices, hospitality, education, healthcare, and safety and emergency sectors. The company holds Cage Code 8Z410 and maintains a National Stock Number reference list for government and defense procurement.

LEDtronics emphasizes its U.S.-based manufacturing heritage, promoting itself as an American LED lighting and indicator expert since 1983. The company’s differentiators include domestic production, a broad cross-reference for incandescent-to-LED conversion, and a focus on markets requiring long-life, ruggedized lighting solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["LED bulb manufacturing", "LED indicator manufacturing", "LED lighting assembly", "PCB LED assembly", "SMD LED assembly", "Panel indicator manufacturing", "Custom LED lighting assemblies"], "industries": ["Industrial Controls", "Defense & Aerospace", "Power Plants & Utilities", "Transportation & Railroad", "Cities & Municipalities", "Elevators & Escalators", "Commercial & Office", "Hospitality", "Education", "Healthcare", "Safety & Emergency", "Government / Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufactures LED products in the USA since 1983", "Cage Code 8Z410 for government and defense supply", "National Stock Number (NSN) part reference list", "Direct LED replacements for miniature and indicator lamps", "Serves defense, aerospace, industrial, transportation, and municipal markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 -> db", "Headquarters Torrance, California -> db", "Cage Code 8Z410 -> /", "Manufactures LED products in USA since 1983 -> /", "Product categories: LED bulbs, indicators, lighting components -> /", "Industries served: Industrial Controls, Defense & Aerospace, Power Plants & Utilities, Transportation & Railroad, Cities & Municipalities, Elevators & Escalators, Commercial & Office, Hospitality, Education, Healthcare, Safety & Emergency -> /", "NSN part number reference for Government/Defense -> /", "Made in USA claim -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a proud American company that has been manufacturing LED products in the USA since 1983!", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "8Z410", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ledtronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LaFrance Fabrics, operating as P&A Industrial Fabrications (PAIF), is headquartered in Pendleton, South Carolina. The company was founded in 1996 and traces its weaving heritage to the velvet looms that have operated in Roxboro, North Carolina, for more than a century. PAIF is a subsidiary of the P&A Group, LLC.

The company manufactures premium woven fabrics on velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms. Its product range includes paint roller fabrics (1/4″ to 3/4″ nap), grip tape roll covering, microfiber cleaning fabrics, automotive heel pads, polyester filtration media, ski climbing skins, flat fabrics, and drop-stitch fabrics for inflatable boats, body boards, and airline lift bags. Finishing capabilities cover tentering, heat setting, coating, napping, shearing, and slitting. The facility serves both domestic and international markets, exporting to ten countries, and relies on a workforce where weavers average 30 years of experience and leadership totals 160 combined years in textiles.

Primary markets include automotive (carpet heel pads, paint roller fabrics), textile (grip tape), marine (inflatable boat fabrics), aerospace and defense (airline lift bags, governmental contracts), filtration, and sports (ski skins). Customers range from professional contractors and DIY consumers to commercial and government agencies.

PAIF differentiates itself through Berry Compliance certification on its velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms, a Lean Manufacturing system with regular 5S and Kaizen events, and a dedicated PhD-led development team that collaborates with customers and suppliers on custom solutions. The company emphasizes long-term relationships and continuous improvement as a strategic supply-chain partner.', certifications=ARRAY['Berry Compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Velvet loom weaving", "Jacquard loom weaving", "Drop-stitch loom weaving", "Tentering", "Heat setting", "Coating", "Napping", "Shearing", "Slitting", "Product development (PhD-led)", "Berry Compliance certification"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Textile", "Marine", "Aerospace & Defense", "Filtration", "Sports & Recreation", "Industrial", "Government"], "materials": ["Velvet", "Microfiber", "Polyester"], "equipment": ["Velvet looms", "Jacquard looms", "Drop-stitch looms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Berry Compliance certification on velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms", "Lean Manufacturing with annual 5S and Kaizen events", "PhD-led product development partnering with customers and suppliers", "Workforce averaging 30 years of weaving experience, leadership with 160 combined years", "Exports to 10 countries"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Pendleton, SC -> db", "Founded in 1996 -> db", "Operates as P&A Industrial Fabrications, part of P&A Group -> /about-us", "Heritage of velvet looms in Roxboro, NC for over 100 years -> /about-us", "Manufactures paint roller fabrics, grip tape, microfiber, automotive heel pads, polyester filtration, ski skins, flat fabrics, drop-stitch fabrics -> /about-us", "Finishing: tentering, heat setting, coating, napping, shearing, slitting -> /about-us", "Berry Compliance certification for velvet, jacquard, drop-stitch looms -> /about-us", "Weavers average 30 years experience, leadership 160 combined years -> /about-us", "Lean Manufacturing, 5S, Kaizen events -> /about-us", "PhD-led development -> /about-us", "Exports to 10 countries -> /about-us", "Industries: automotive, textile, marine, aerospace/defense, filtration, sports -> /about-us", "Equipment: velvet looms, jacquard looms, drop-stitch looms -> /about-us", "Materials: velvet, microfiber, polyester -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "P&A Industrial Fabrications (PAIF) has been supplying premium woven fabrics for the US and currently exports into 10 countries.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='la-france-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LaMar Plastics & Displays, Ltd. is a family-owned and operated manufacturer based in Freeport, New York. Founded in 1965, the company has served the plastic packaging and point-of-purchase display industry from its New York facility for decades.

The company operates an expansive facility housing ten automatic in-line vacuum forming machines, two large sample machines, four 5'' x 10'' CNC router tables with tool changers, two HAAS CNC milling machines for aluminum vacuum form tooling, and a 6'' x 10'' 400-watt CNC laser cutter. Additional capabilities include in-house silk screening, RF sealing for clamshell packaging, heat bending of plastics and acrylics, and flatbed digital printing on woods, plastics, acrylics, and PETG. LaMar provides end-to-end services from CAD design and prototyping through manufacturing, decorating (hot stamping, silk screening, stitching, labeling), and shipping.

LaMar serves the cosmetic, liquor, and retail industries, producing point-of-purchase displays, clamshell packaging, ESD and anti-static trays for sensitive electronics, and blister trays. The company also works with smaller startup customers, offering design, prototyping, and quick sample turnaround.

The company emphasizes a one-stop-shop model, combining design, prototyping, manufacturing, and shipping under one roof, with a commitment to evolving technology and fast, affordable service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum forming", "CNC router cutting", "CNC laser cutting", "CNC milling (aluminum tooling)", "Silk screening", "RF sealing", "Heat bending", "Flatbed digital printing", "CAD design", "Prototyping", "Assembly", "Contract packaging", "Hot stamping", "Stitching", "Labeling", "Edge banding", "Painting and staining"], "industries": ["Cosmetic", "Liquor", "Retail", "Electronics", "Advertising and display", "Point-of-purchase display", "Packaging"], "materials": ["Polystyrene", "Anti-static plastics", "ESD plastics", "PETG", "RPET", "PVC", "Wood", "Melamine", "Acrylic", "MDF", "Sintra", "Foam", "Recycled styrene"], "equipment": ["10 automatic in-line vacuum forming machines", "2 large vacuum forming sample machines", "4 5'' x 10'' flat bed router tables with tool changers", "2 HAAS CNC milling machines", "1 6'' x 10'' x 400W laser cutting machine", "Automatic edge banding machines", "RF sealing machines", "Custom made heat bending machine", "Flatbed digital printing machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.002 in kerf for laser cutting", "built_on": ["Ten automatic in-line vacuum forming machines enabling competitive pricing", "One-stop-shop for design, prototyping, manufacturing, and shipping", "In-house CAD and computer rendering for rapid prototyping", "Flatbed digital printing added in 2020 on woods, plastics, acrylics, PETG", "Fast sample turnaround for startup customers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> /", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters Freeport, NY -> db", "Industries: cosmetic, liquor, retail -> /", "Vacuum forming machines (10 automatic in-line, 2 sample) -> /services", "CNC router tables (4) -> /services", "HAAS milling machines (2) -> /services", "Laser cutter (6''x10'' 400W) -> /services", "Silk screening, RF sealing, heat bending -> /services", "Flatbed digital printing (2020) -> /services", "CAD design, prototyping, assembly, packaging -> /", "Materials: polystyrene, anti-static, ESD, PETG, RPET, PVC, wood, melamine, acrylic, MDF, Sintra, foam, recycled styrene -> /, /services", "Laser kerf 0.002\" -> /services", "One-stop-shop model -> /", "Fast sample turnaround -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LaMar Plastics is a family-owned and operated company serving the Plastic Packaging and P.O.P. Display industry since 1965 in our New York facility.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lamar-plastics-displays-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lacerta Group, LLC. is headquartered in Mansfield, Massachusetts, and traces its roots to 1993 when the Lotfi family founded the company in Boston’s empowerment zone. The business began as a thermoforming operation that quickly incorporated recycled plastic material. In 2020, the Lotfi family sold a majority stake to SK Capital Partners but remained involved in strategy and operations.

The company manufactures thermoformed PET packaging for food applications, offering both stock and custom solutions. Its fully integrated platform covers in-house design, tooling, printing, and film-sealable and tamper-evident formats. Lacerta operates seven U.S. facilities — three in Mansfield, plus sites in Chatsworth, California; Attleboro, Massachusetts; and Portage, Wisconsin — and maintains an on-site warehouse for immediate shipment of hundreds of stock items. The company reports having recycled more than 150 million pounds of plastic since inception and holds SQF certification for food packaging manufacturing.

Lacerta serves commercial food producers, supermarkets, and convenience-store chains, supplying containers for grab-and-go items such as sandwiches, salads, snacks, and prepared meals. Its packaging is designed to extend shelf life and provide crystal-clear product visibility.

The company differentiates itself through its ReCERTA™ material, which guarantees an average of at least 10% post-consumer recycled content across all PET products, with custom blends available. Lacerta also emphasizes speed to market, sustainability consulting (including life-cycle assessments), and a partnership model that spans the entire product lifecycle.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF certification in Manufacturing of Food Packaging']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoforming", "PET packaging", "Sustainable packaging", "In-house design", "Custom packaging", "Stock packaging", "Film-sealable packaging", "Tamper-evident packaging", "Printing", "Packaging design", "Life cycle assessment", "Brand messaging", "Packaging insights", "Custom PCR blends", "Post-consumer recycled content integration", "SQF-certified food packaging manufacturing"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Commercial food producers", "Supermarkets", "Convenience stores", "Grab-and-go foodservice", "Prepared foods", "Sandwiches", "Salads", "Snacks"], "materials": ["PET", "Post-consumer recycled plastic (PCR)", "ReCERTA\u2122 material"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SQF certification in Manufacturing of Food Packaging", "ReCERTA\u2122 material with \u226510% PCR content across PET products", "Fully integrated manufacturing platform (design, tooling, printing, thermoforming)", "Seven U.S. facilities with on-site warehouse for same-day stock shipment", "In-house design and sustainability consulting (life-cycle assessment, brand messaging)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993 in Boston, Massachusetts -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Mansfield, Massachusetts -> /about-us", "Operates seven U.S. facilities (three in Mansfield, one in Chatsworth CA, one in Attleboro MA, one in Portage WI) -> /about-us", "Founded by Lotfi family -> /about-us", "Became portfolio company of SK Capital Partners in 2020 -> /about-us", "Recycled over 150 million pounds of plastic material since 1993 -> /about-us", "SQF certification in Manufacturing of Food Packaging -> /about-us", "Offers thermoformed PET packaging, sustainable packaging, in-house design -> /about-us", "Serves commercial food producers and supermarkets -> /about-us", "ReCERTA\u2122 material with average at least 10% PCR content -> /about-us", "Stock packaging ready to ship from on-site warehouse -> /about-us", "Custom packaging process from design to printing -> /about-us", "Speed to market, innovation, partnership model -> /about-us", "Sustainability consulting including life cycle assessment and brand messaging -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Providing high-quality thermoformed plastic packaging to customers across the country for more than 30 years.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lacerta-group-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LadyBug Technologies, LLC is headquartered in Boise, Idaho, after relocating from Santa Rosa, California in 2021. The company was founded in 2004 by two microwave engineers, Richard Hawkins and Jon Sigler, who shared a passion for quality microwave test instrumentation. Hawkins serves as president, bringing four decades of RF and microwave test and measurement experience from Sonoma County, while Sigler, a retired vice president and U.S. Marine veteran with calibration lab experience, contributed software and firmware expertise.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures a broad line of USB power sensors that function as complete, self-contained power measurement solutions without a separate power meter. Its portfolio spans True RMS, peak/pulse/average, pulse profiling, and small form factor sensors covering 4 kHz to 67 GHz with 86 dB dynamic range. The LB5900 series adds optional I2C and SPI connectivity and Linux compatibility. LadyBug also operates a calibration service providing NIST-traceable certificates, a power sensor rental program, and accessories. The 2021 move to Boise doubled the facility footprint, increased manufacturing capacity by 30%, and expanded the product engineering team.

LadyBug’s sensors serve general-purpose RF power testing, automated test equipment (ATE), defense, and portable or compact applications across the microwave and RF test industry.

The company was created to deliver a better product at a better price, built in the U.S.A. Its patented NoZero NoCal technology eliminates user zeroing before measurement, reduces the need for switches and cables in low-level ATE setups, and provides thermal stabilization to prevent drift. The integrated sensor architecture removes the uncertainty of a separate meter and consolidates calibration into a single device.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS-3 compliance','REACH compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["USB power sensor design and manufacturing", "True RMS power measurement", "Peak, pulse, and average power measurement", "Pulse profiling", "Small form factor sensor design", "LAN-compatible sensor integration", "I2C and SPI interface development", "NIST-traceable calibration services", "Power sensor rental program", "Calibration certificate generation", "Product certificate of compliance", "REACH and RoHS compliance documentation", "Conflict minerals reporting (CMRT)"], "industries": ["RF and microwave test and measurement", "Automated test equipment (ATE)", "Defense and aerospace", "Wireless communications", "Radar and electronic warfare", "Satellite systems", "General purpose RF power testing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2004 in Santa Rosa, CA -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Boise, ID since 2021 move -> /about-us", "Founders: Richard Hawkins (President) and Jon Sigler (retired VP, co-founder) -> /about-us", "Jon Sigler U.S. Marine calibration lab tour -> /about-us", "2021 move doubled space, added 30% manufacturing capacity, expanded engineering team -> /about-us", "Manufactures USB power sensors 4 kHz\u201367 GHz, 86 dB dynamic range -> /", "Sensor types: True RMS, peak/pulse/average, pulse profiling, small form factor, LAN compatible -> /", "LB5900 series with I2C/SPI, Linux compatible -> /", "Patented NoZero NoCal feature eliminates zeroing, thermally stabilized -> /", "Integrated self-contained sensor architecture -> /", "Calibration services with NIST-traceable certificates -> /quality", "Power sensor rental program -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "RoHS-3, REACH, CMRT compliance -> /quality", "Industries: general RF testing, ATE, defense, portable/compact, microwave/RF test -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LadyBug Technologies designs, develops, and manufactures a broad range of first tier NIST traceable USB power sensors.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ladybug-technologies-llc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ladybug-technologies-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lakeside Metal Fabrication, LLC was founded in 2000 in Mena, Arkansas, and has served Polk County and the surrounding region for over two decades.

The shop provides a range of metalworking services, including welding, sheet metal work, and custom fabrication for projects both simple and complex. It also operates a trailer repair and service department, sells trailer parts and accessories, towing accessories, truck accessories, and offers hitch installation and truck bed sales and service. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are published.

Lakeside Metal Fabrication serves individual vehicle owners, local businesses, and commercial fleets needing trailer maintenance, custom metal components, or truck accessory installation. The company describes its customer base as spanning various industries, though specific sectors are not named.

The company emphasizes its "Fabrication Done Right" motto, citing over 30 years of combined experience and a track record of helping more than 4,000 clients. It highlights skilled craftsmen who ensure precision and full compliance with applicable standards.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Welding", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Custom metal fabrication", "Trailer repair and service", "Trailer parts and accessories sales", "Towing accessories sales", "Truck accessories sales", "Hitch installation", "Truck bed sales and service"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Fabrication Done Right\" quality commitment", "Over 30 years of combined experience", "4,000+ clients served", "Skilled craftsmen ensuring precision and compliance", "Local service across Polk County and surrounding areas"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> db, /about-us", "Headquartered in Mena, Arkansas -> db, /about-us", "Offers welding, sheet metal, custom fabrication -> /", "Provides trailer repair, parts, accessories -> /", "Offers hitch installation, truck bed sales -> /", "Over 30 years experience, 4,000+ clients helped -> /about-us", "Fabrication Done Right motto -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "WELDING | SHEET METAL | CUSTOM FABRICATION | TRAILER REPAIR + SERVICE | TRAILER PARTS + ACCESSORIES | TOWING ACCESSORIES | TRUCK ACCESSORIES | HITCH INSTALLS | TRUCK BED SALES + SERVICE", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lakeside-metal-fabrication-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lakeside Trading LLC has operated from Narragansett, Rhode Island since 1999, when founder Dave Harrigan liquidated his 401(k) to purchase a trailer load of hand-made clay chimineas from Mexico. The family-owned business began as a wholesale and seasonal market venture before Harrigan encountered Pennsylvania shed builders during East Coast buying trips. Recognizing a gap in the Rhode Island market, he acquired a shed-moving trailer and leased a former 19th-century fishing equipment warehouse on South Pier Road, establishing a permanent location that he purchased outright in 2010.

Today the company maintains a 5,000-square-foot showroom and an expansive display yard staffed by 20 full-time employees, several with more than 15 years of tenure. Lakeside Trading does not manufacture its own products; instead it procures, installs, and services American-made sheds, greenhouses, chicken coops, gazebos, garages, pergolas, playsets, and pavilions, along with outdoor furniture crafted from recycled plastic poly lumber and marine-grade hardware. The team installs more than 1,000 structures and sells over 2,000 furniture pieces each year, and also provides site preparation such as gravel or stone pads, rock pads, and shed relocation services.

The primary customer base is residential homeowners throughout Rhode Island seeking durable outdoor storage and living solutions. Projects range from simple garden sheds and Adirondack chairs to custom-designed pavilions, greenhouses converted into art studios, and chicken coops with epoxy floors and automatic doors. The company also handles used-shed purchases, moving and reinstalling them on prepared foundations.

Lakeside Trading differentiates itself through Amish-crafted structures backed by a 10-year warranty and a lifetime service guarantee, free on-site consultations before purchase, and a commitment to fair pricing. The business remains locally owned and operated, emphasizing personal service from sales through installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shed and outdoor structure installation", "Site preparation and foundation work (gravel/stone pads, rock pads)", "Shed moving and relocation", "Custom design consultation for sheds and structures", "Retail sales of American-made sheds, outdoor furniture, greenhouses, chicken coops, gazebos, garages, pergolas, playsets, pavilions"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Shed-moving trailer", "Mule (utility vehicle)", "Flatbed truck"], "volume": "1,000+ structures installed annually; 2,000+ furniture pieces sold annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Amish-crafted structures with 10-year warranty and lifetime service guarantee", "Free on-site consultations before purchase", "Family-owned and operated in Rhode Island since 1999", "5,000 sqft showroom with large display yard", "Installation services including shed moving, site leveling, and foundation work"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 by Dave Harrigan -> /about", "Family-owned, locally operated -> /, /about", "5,000 sqft showroom at 326 South Pier Road -> /, /about", "20 full-time staff, some 15+ years -> /about", "Installs 1,000+ structures annually, sells 2,000+ furniture pieces -> /about", "Products: sheds, greenhouses, chicken coops, gazebos, garages, pergolas, playsets, pavilions, outdoor furniture -> /, /about", "Amish-crafted structures, 10-year warranty, lifetime service guarantee -> /", "Free on-site consultations -> /", "Shed-moving trailer, mule, flatbed truck -> /, /about", "Materials: recycled plastic poly lumber, marine-grade hardware, pressure-treated pine, cedar, vinyl -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a locally owned and operated company located in Narragansett, Rhode Island. For over 25 years, our talented team has procured, installed, and serviced high-quality American-made sheds, outdoor structures, greenhouses, furniture, and more.", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "20 full-time staff", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lakeside-trading-sheds-outdoor-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lance Industries has been building vacuum meat tumblers in Hartford, Wisconsin since 1985. The company was founded to give U.S. meat processors a durable, reliable alternative to imported equipment, becoming the first American-made meat tumbler on the market. Its designs originated from collaboration with Family Farms Meats and the engineering staff at LMI Manufacturing.

The product line comprises four models ranging from 50 to 1,000 pounds of capacity: the LT-5, LT-15, LT-30, and LT-60. Each unit features variable-speed rotation, a digital timer, built-in vacuum, and wheels that allow it to pass through a standard 32-inch door. Drums are constructed from thicker-gauge steel with removable lids and metal-detectable gaskets for sanitation. More than 3,000 tumblers have been installed worldwide, and the company maintains a fully stocked service and repair department.

Customers include meat markets, grocery stores, butcher shops, delis, restaurants, meat processing facilities, and meat-alternative processors. Testimonials cite operations such as Haun''s Meat & Sausage, Bardini''s Country Smokehouse, Bob''s Processing, Hudson Meats, and Quality Cut Meats. Lance also works with domestic and international dealers and participates in the American Association of Meat Processors and the Wisconsin Association of Meat Processors.

