UPDATE companies SET description='Larson Cable Trailers, Inc. was founded in 2000 by Rick Larson in Huron, South Dakota. The company originated from Larson''s underground utilities business, Larson Digging Inc., where he needed a trailer that could lift cable reels, "figure 8," and rewind cable efficiently. Unable to find a suitable solution, he engineered his own patented cable fiber installation trailer. In 2024, the business was acquired by Felling Trailers and continues to operate as a separate division, leveraging the resources of a full-line trailer manufacturer with over 240 models.

The company manufactures patented reel-handling trailers designed for fiber-optic and power utility installations. Its core product line includes trailers that combine reel lifting, figure-8 cable layout, and rewinding in a single unit. Early that year, the division expanded its portfolio with the addition of the Drive Trailers product line, broadening its range of trailer solutions.

Customers include public and private contractors, rural telephone cooperatives, electric cooperatives, and city municipalities across the United States. The equipment is used by firms such as K&H Electric Inc. of Linton, North Dakota, which cited the trailer''s versatility in eliminating the need for multiple separate machines.

Larson''s founding premise was to solve a real-world problem: existing trailers could not perform the combined functions required for efficient cable installation. The company emphasizes patented designs that improve crew productivity, durability in harsh conditions, and reliability that helps crews lay more cable in less time. Its stated mission is to drive efficiency and innovation in cable installation by working directly with installation crews to refine equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable fiber installation trailer manufacturing", "Reel handling and figure-8 cable layout", "Cable rewinding equipment", "Trailer parts distribution", "Warranty and manual support", "Online parts sales", "Drive Trailer manufacturing"], "industries": ["Fiber-optic installation", "Power utility installation", "Telecommunications", "Electrical contracting", "Rural telephone cooperatives", "Electric cooperatives", "Municipal infrastructure"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented cable fiber installation trailer with integrated figure-8 and rewind functions", "Operates as a division of Felling Trailers, accessing 240+ trailer models", "Online parts store offering manuals, warranty service, and replacement components", "Drive Trailers product line added in 2024 to serve broader applications", "Designed from hands-on underground utility experience for real-world conditions"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 by Rick Larson -> /about", "Headquarters in Huron, South Dakota -> db", "Acquired by Felling Trailers, operates as separate division -> /about", "Patented cable fiber installation trailer design -> /", "Serves public/private contractors, rural telephone co-ops, electric cooperatives, city municipalities -> /about", "Added Drive Trailers product line in early 2024 -> /about", "Online parts store for trailer parts, manuals, warranty services -> /", "Customer testimonial from Mylo Kramer, Owner K&H Electric Inc. -> /", "Mission: driving efficiency and innovation in cable installation -> /about", "Rick Larson founded company after unable to find suitable trailer for his underground utilities business Larson Digging Inc. -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Larson Cable Trailers revolutionized the industry as the original creator of the patented cable fiber installation trailer.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='larson-cable-trailers-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Murrieta, California, Latest Metalworks, Inc. was founded nearly two decades ago with a mission to bring clients'' visions to life through custom metal fabrication. The company operates from Riverside County and serves customers nationally.

The shop provides full-program fabrication from engineering review through final delivery. Core processes include flat and tube laser cutting on an AMADA fiberoptic system, waterjet cutting on an OMAX machine, forming and bending on an Amada press brake, 8-axis tube bending and rolling, LADBS-certified welding, and in-house engineering using SolidWorks. Secondary finishing, fitment, assembly, and a dedicated packaging department support production runs, structural assemblies, exhibit structures, prototype programs, and architectural metalwork.

Latest Metalworks serves automotive OEM, industrial, architectural, EV and solar, and R&D sectors, with documented work for aerospace suppliers and municipal water departments. Clients include the Temeka Group for retail and museum projects, the City of Oceanside Water Department for plant maintenance, Inokinetic for aerospace components, and tooling firms such as Tube Bending Technology and V&T Tooling.

The company emphasizes combining traditional craftsmanship with current technology, citing its ISO 9001:2015 certification and LADBS structural steel fabricator approval as foundations for quality. A problem-solving, forward-thinking mindset and in-house equipment aim to reduce lead times and control quality from prototype to production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','LADBS Structural Steel Fabricator Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Laser cutting (flat)", "Tube laser cutting", "Waterjet cutting", "Forming & bending (press brake)", "Tube bending & rolling (8-axis)", "Welding (LADBS certified)", "Engineering & design (SolidWorks)", "Secondary finishing", "Packaging & kitting", "Fitment & assembly", "Structural steel fabrication", "Prototyping", "Production runs", "Architectural metalwork", "Exhibit structures"], "industries": ["Automotive OEM", "Industrial", "Architectural", "EV & Solar", "R&D", "Aerospace", "Municipal/Water treatment", "Retail/Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["OMAX waterjet", "AMADA fiberoptic laser", "Amada press brake"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified (certificate #1120219)", "LADBS certified structural steel fabricator (#FB03359)", "In-house AMADA fiberoptic laser for rapid turnaround", "OMAX waterjet for cutting a wide range of materials and thicknesses", "8-axis precision tube bending and rolling capability"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location: Latest Metalworks, Inc., Murrieta, California -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certification (#1120219) -> /", "LADBS Structural Steel Fabricator certification (#FB03359) -> /", "Founded nearly two decades ago with mission to bring clients'' visions to life -> /about", "Core processes: laser cutting, waterjet cutting, forming/bending, tube bending/rolling, welding, engineering, finishing, packaging -> / and /services", "Equipment: AMADA fiberoptic laser, OMAX waterjet, Amada press brake -> 