UPDATE companies SET description='LeVic Plastics was founded in 1971 by Leslie "Bill" Stober and Vic Mathis in a garage in Grandview, Missouri, as a prototype molding operation. The company incorporated and moved to Grandview, where Ron Knight became a partial owner and later sole owner in 1990; Bob Knight purchased the business in a later transition.

The company provides custom plastic injection molding, mold design, in-house tooling, and secondary operations under one roof. Its facility houses 10 Shibaura (Toshiba) presses ranging from 55 to 250 tons, capable of holding tolerances to ±0.001 inch and running volumes from a single piece to more than 100,000 parts. Secondary services include sonic welding, hot stamping, pad printing, assembly, and packaging.

LeVic serves manufacturers in medical, aerospace, electronics, oil and gas, industrial automation, machinery, and packaging sectors. The firm works with commodity thermoplastics, engineering-grade resins, reinforced materials, and custom color-matched formulations, and offers insert molding as a standard capability.

LeVic emphasizes a "One-Vendor Advantage," managing the entire process from design-for-manufacturability review through tooling, molding, and finishing to eliminate multi-supplier coordination. The company holds ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certifications, imposes no minimum order quantities, and returns standard quotes within two to three business days.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mold Design", "In-house Tooling", "Custom Plastic Injection Molding", "Secondary Operations & Assembly", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Full 3D CAD capabilities (SolidWorks, Mastercam)", "Prototype & production tooling design", "Aluminum molds", "Steel molds", "Prototype tooling", "Production tooling", "CNC machining", "Mold modifications", "Insert molding", "Color matching", "Sonic welding", "Hot stamping", "Pad printing", "Assembly services", "Packaging"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Electronics", "Oil & Gas", "Industrial Automation", "Machinery", "Packaging"], "materials": ["Commodity thermoplastics", "Engineering-grade thermoplastics", "Reinforced materials", "Insert molding", "Custom color matching"], "equipment": ["10 Shibaura (Toshiba) injection molding presses (55\u2013250 ton)"], "volume": "1 to 100,000+ pieces", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 inch", "built_on": ["One vendor manages mold design, tooling, molding, and secondary operations", "No minimum order quantities", "ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certified", "Tolerances held to \u00b10.001 inch", "Standard quotes returned in 2\u20133 business days"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 by Leslie ''Bill'' Stober and Vic Mathis -> /about", "Headquarters Grandview, Missouri -> /about, /", "Ron Knight sole owner 1990, Bob Knight later owner -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certified -> /, /services", "10 Shibaura (Toshiba) presses 55-250 ton -> /, /services", "Tolerances \u00b10.001 inch -> /, /services", "Volume 1 to 100,000+ pieces -> /, /servic