UPDATE companies SET description='Leprino Foods Company began in 1950 when Mike Leprino Sr. started making mozzarella cheese in the back room of his family''s corner grocery store at 38th Avenue and Shoshone Street in Denver, Colorado. The business incorporated as Leprino Cheese Manufacturing Company in the 1960s and was renamed Leprino Foods Company in the 1970s to reflect its expanding portfolio. It remains family-owned today.

The company produces mozzarella and pizza cheese, whey protein, lactose, micellar casein, and other dairy ingredients. Its patented "Same Day Dice" process turns fresh milk into cheese in four hours, and its Quality-Locked Cheese uses individual quick freezing to preserve flavor. Operations span manufacturing facilities on three continents, including a 640,000-square-foot plant in Lemoore, California, with over 1,100 employees, and a new $1 billion facility in Lubbock, Texas. Global headcount exceeds 5,000.

Leprino supplies food and nutrition brands worldwide, including major pizza chains, with products sold in more than 70 countries.

