UPDATE companies SET description='Liberate Medical is based in Crestwood, Kentucky. The company develops the VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator, a medical device designed to address respiratory muscle atrophy in mechanically ventilated patients.

The VentFree system uses proprietary non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation to contract the abdominal wall muscles in synchrony with exhalation during mechanical ventilation. Therapy can begin from day one of ventilation while patients are sedated or delirious, and the device is described as quick and simple to use. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are disclosed.

The company serves the critical care and respiratory care segments of the healthcare industry. Its customers include hospitals and ICU teams managing mechanically ventilated patients, particularly those requiring more than four days of ventilation who face high rates of weaning failure and post-discharge complications.

Liberate Medical states that its approach may reduce abdominal muscle atrophy and shorten the duration of mechanical ventilation. A pilot randomized controlled trial found that ventilation duration and ICU length of stay were shorter in patients receiving VentFree stimulation compared to placebo, potentially reducing morbidity, mortality, and healthcare costs.', certifications=ARRAY['CE Mark']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation", "Ventilator-synchronized respiratory muscle stimulation", "Medical device development for critical care", "Clinical trial execution (pilot RCT)", "Regulatory compliance (CE Mark, FDA EUA)"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Healthcare", "Critical Care", "Respiratory Care"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation synchronized with exhalation", "Therapy can begin from day one of mechanical ventilation while patients are sedated or delirious", "CE marked for sale in the European Economic Area", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization for reducing disuse atrophy in adult ventilated patients, including COVID-19"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Crestwood, Kentucky -> db", "Product: VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator -> /", "Technology: Non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation synchronized with exhalation -> /", "Therapy can begin day one of ventilation while sedated/delirious -> /", "CE marked for European Economic Area -> /", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization for COVID-19 related ventilation -> /", "Pilot RCT showed reduced ventilation duration and ICU stay -> /", "Certification: CE MARKED -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator uses proprietary non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation to contract the abdominal wall muscles in synchrony with exhalation during mechanical ventilation.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["CE Mark (European Economic Area)", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization (USA)"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='liberate-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lincoln Electric Products Co. has operated from Union, New Jersey since its founding in 1949. The company began as a manufacturer of electrical distribution equipment serving the tri-state region, built on the core values established by founder Irving Leff. Today it remains a family-owned and operated business, led by President Matthew Leff, with ownership and management continuing along the same lines set at inception.

The company produces a full range of highly customizable electrical distribution equipment, including switchboards and integrated electrical systems. All equipment is manufactured in the United States under an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system. The firm emphasizes a design and integration process supported by experienced project managers and engineers, targeting lead times as short as four weeks while maintaining cost efficiency. An two-year warranty covers all equipment.

Customers span the tri-state area and include businesses and institutions that require reliable power infrastructure with minimal downtime. The company describes its solutions as the backbone of reliable power for operations that cannot afford interruption, serving industries, businesses, and communities with tailored electrical distribution products.

The company states its differentiation rests on precision craftsmanship, dependable performance, and customer-focused service — values traced to its founding. Ongoing investment in advanced technologies and efficient manufacturing processes is cited as the means to stay ahead of industry demands, with a mission to develop collaborative, trusting relationships and produce reliable, well-engineered, high-quality electrical equipment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom electrical distribution equipment manufacturing", "Switchboard manufacturing", "Electrical system design and integration", "Project management", "Engineering design", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "as short as four weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned continuity since 1949", "All equipment manufactured in the USA", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "Two-year warranty on all equipment", "Target lead times as short as four weeks"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1949 -> /about", "Family-owned, founder Irving Leff -> /about", "Headquarters Union, New Jersey -> db, /about", "President Matthew Leff -> /about", "Manufactures customizable electrical distribution equipment, switchboards -> /, /quality", "All equipment manufactured in USA -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Two-year warranty on all equipment -> /, /quality", "Target lead times as short as four weeks -> /", "Serves tri-state area, businesses needing reliable power -> /, /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build a full range of highly customizable electrical distribution equipment.", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lincoln-electric-products-co' AND a