UPDATE companies SET description='Lincoln Industries operates from Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin, where it has built a privately held metal finishing business spanning more than seven decades. The company describes itself as the largest and most diverse privately held metal finisher in North America, though it does not disclose a founding year or founder names in its public materials.

In recent years the company has broadened its truck-component portfolio beyond exhaust systems to include bumpers, internal cab parts, grab bars, engine components, emblems, and heat-management solutions, leveraging automation to handle complexity. A 2025 launch added a Fourth Wall division that supplies LED display systems for sports venues, commercial installations, and outdoor environments.

Customers come from agriculture, automotive, appliances, motorsports, powersports, oil and gas, tools, and heavy-duty truck sectors.

