UPDATE companies SET description='Little Homestead Furniture was founded in 1987 by a local architect in Rockville, Maryland. The independent retailer operates a showroom in the Washington, D.C. metropolitan area, specializing in solid American hardwood furniture sourced from domestic manufacturers.

The store carries bedroom, dining, living room, home office, TV/media, and youth bedroom collections. Its inventory is produced by a network of small family-owned factories in New England—particularly Vermont—and additional manufacturing partners in Pennsylvania, Ohio, Indiana, Texas, North Carolina, and Virginia. All pieces are built from solid hardwoods such as cherry, maple, oak, and walnut, and the company offers a made-to-order program that allows dimensional changes, stain adjustments, and feature modifications often at little or no extra cost.

Little Homestead primarily serves residential customers in the D.C. region who favor classic, timeless designs—Shaker, Mission, Arts & Crafts, and contemporary motifs—and who prioritize well-made, domestically produced furniture over mass-market alternatives.

The business positions itself as an antidote to the ubiquitous “distressed” and “weathered” finishes common at large retailers, emphasizing responsibly harvested lumber, traditional joinery (dovetailed drawers, mortise-and-tenon construction), and durable, environmentally friendly finishes. The made-to-order flexibility is cited as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of solid hardwood furniture", "Custom furniture ordering", "Made-to-order modifications", "Showroom consultation"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Cherry", "Maple", "Oak", "Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made-to-order modifications often at no or minimal extra cost", "Responsibly harvested domestic hardwoods", "Traditional joinery including dovetailed drawers and mortise-and-tenon construction", "Environmentally friendly finishes", "Showroom in Rockville, Maryland"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db, homepage", "Headquarters Rockville, Maryland -> db, about-us page", "Founded by a local architect -> about-us page", "Operates as a furniture store -> about-us page", "Manufacturing partners in Vermont, Pennsylvania, Ohio, Indiana, Texas, North Carolina, Virginia -> about-us page", "Offers solid cherry, maple, oak, walnut -> about-us page", "Made-to-order modifications at minimal extra cost -> about-us page", "Caters to DC area customers seeking classic designs -> about-us page", "Construction details: dovetailed drawers, mortise and tenon joinery -> about-us page", "Environmentally friendly finishes -> about-us page", "Showroom in Rockville, Maryland -> about-us page"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Little Homestead is a unique furniture store founded by a local architect nearly 40 years ago offering high quality North American furniture for the Bedroom, Dining Room, Living Room, Home Office, TV/Media, Youth Bedrooms, and more.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='little-homestead-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Loftis Steel & Aluminum, Inc. is a family-owned metals distributor and processor based in Nashville, Tennessee. The company was founded in 2000 as a family business and has since formed a dynamic partnership with Tennessee Die Supply, operating from a Nashville facility that serves the Southeast region. The company describes its legacy as one of resilience, growth, and deep industry roots.

The company supplies a range of metals including aluminum, tool steels, and other alloys, and provides advanced processing services such as precision laser cutting, waterjet cutting, and CAD design support. Its in-house team includes four CAD engineers who assist with design work, print clean-up, and expert guidance. Loftis also operates its own delivery fleet alongside shipping partners to serve customers across the region.

Loftis serves a broad set of industries including aerospace, automotive, construction, energy, firearms, government, machine shops, general manufacturing, medical, and oil & gas. Its customers range from local machine shops and auto parts manufacturers to government agencies, with the company positioning itself as a specialist in each sector.

