UPDATE companies SET description='Lone Mountain Biotechnology and Medical Devices, Inc. was founded in December 2008 by Dr. Robert L. Garnick in Las Vegas, Nevada. Dr. Garnick, who spent 25 years Genentech''s regulatory and quality organizations and contributed to the approval of more than 17 drugs, established the firm to provide specialized consulting and development services to the pharmaceutical and medical device sectors.

The company offers a range of consulting services spanning clinical and CMC regulatory affairs, quality control and assurance, cGXP compliance (including GCP, GLP, and GMP), promotional material review, manufacturing site evaluations, comparability studies, FDA advisory committee preparation, and validation strategy. In addition, Lone Mountain provides experimental and prototype-level device development using AutoCAD and CNC prototyping on Haas equipment, as well as prototype-to-manufacturing strategic planning.

Clients include large pharmaceutical companies, small start-ups, and investors seeking due diligence reviews. Over a recent year, the firm worked with more than 15 clients and facilitated numerous FDA Type C meetings. It has also supported three biosimilar development programs, assisting with cell line and process development.

Lone Mountain differentiates itself through its network of senior consultants—many of whom collaborated with Dr. Garnick at Genentech—providing clients with a "Dream Team" that has collectively brought over 17 drugs to market. The firm emphasizes rapid, collaborative resolution of complex drug development issues and regulatory challenges.', certifications=ARRAY['GMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Regulatory affairs consulting (IND, NDA, BLA, CTX preparation and review)", "Quality control and assurance for drugs, biologics, and devices", "cGXP compliance (GCP, GLP, GMP)", "Promotional material review", "Manufacturing site evaluations for IND/NDA/BLA applications", "Comparability study design and execution", "FDA advisory committee planning and rehearsals", "Validation strategy for analytical methods and manufacturing processes", "cGXP/cGMP/cGLP inspectional support", "Strategy development for new manufacturing sites", "FDA/EMEA review interaction management", "Medical device development strategy and execution", "AutoCAD device development to G-code", "Prototype device design and development", "Prototype-to-manufacturing strategic planning", "Due diligence reviews of manufacturing capabilities and capacities", "Due diligence reviews of CMC sections of CTDs", "Warning letter and consent decree evaluation and resolution", "Clinical trial design and implementation", "Pre-clinical studies", "Process sciences and analytical methods development", "GXP compliance consulting", "Stability studies", "Virology and microbiology consulting"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Biotechnology", "Medical Device"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Haas CNC equipment", "AutoCAD"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Access to a \"Dream Team\" of consultants with a collective track record of 17+ drug approvals over 25 years", "Facilitation of FDA Type C meetings for early-stage drug development programs", "Proven experience in biosimilar cell line and pr