UPDATE companies SET description='MCS Woodworking LLC was founded in 1995 in Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin, to serve architects, designers, and contractors with custom millwork, cabinetry, and architectural woodworking.

Operating from a 20,000-square-foot facility in Menomonee Falls, the company combines traditional woodworking techniques with modern millwork technology, including CAD-based cost engineering and state-of-the-art tools. MCS Woodworking produces custom cabinetry, commercial millwork, architectural woodworking, and specialty items such as church furnishings, corporate office fixtures, and retail displays. The firm reports more than 3,000 completed commercial projects, ranging from one-of-a-kind builds to large-scale construction solutions.

The company serves a broad range of industries, including commercial, architectural, religious, corporate office, education, healthcare, hospitality, restaurant, and retail sectors. Its client base comprises architects, designers, general contractors, and business owners. Notable projects include the St. James 1868 Milwaukee Event Center, where MCS contributed intricate millwork, historic trim reproductions, staircases, and decorative railings; the IMPROV of Brookfield, featuring casework, decorative trim, upholstered wooden booths, and solid surface countertops; and the Fox Point Lutheran Church, with updates to sanctuary, offices, and atrium.

MCS Woodworking emphasizes a proven process that spans initial consultation, design and planning, precision crafting, and professional installation. The company highlights its dedication to building lasting partnerships, getting projects right the first time, and meeting tight deadlines. It has been recognized multiple times in Wood & Wood Products Magazine''s WOOD 100 Report as one of the nation''s fastest-growing woodworking companies.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Commercial millwork", "Architectural woodworking", "Custom woodworking", "Church woodworking (pews, altars, pulpits, baptismal fonts)", "Classic woodworking (traditional joinery, heirloom-quality construction)", "Corporate office woodworking (reception desks, workstations, storage)", "Education woodworking (library shelving, circulation desks, laboratory casework)", "Healthcare woodworking (nurses'' stations, patient room cabinetry, antimicrobial finishes)", "Hospitality woodworking (lobby reception desks, bar fronts, guest room casegoods)", "Restaurant woodworking (custom bars, banquette seating, host stands, dining tables)", "Retail store woodworking (cash wraps, display cases, shelving units, fitting rooms)", "CAD-based design and cost engineering", "Professional installation", "Custom mouldings and trim reproduction", "Staircase fabrication", "Decorative railings", "Solid surface countertop integration", "Upholstered wooden booth fabrication", "Commercial-grade protective coatings"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Architectural", "Religious/Church", "Corporate Office", "Education", "Healthcare", "Hospitality", "Restaurant", "Retail"], "materials": ["Wood species (various)", "Finishes (various)", "Solid surface materials", "Antimicrobial finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["20,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Menomonee Falls, WI", "CAD-based cost engineering and state-of-the-art tooling"