UPDATE companies SET description='MPC Design Technologies, Inc. is headquartered in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company traces its roots to the early 1990s when its founder, a seasoned PCB designer, left his employer after being passed over for a promotion and decided to start his own firm. Since inception, the business has expanded to include experienced professionals across design, assembly, and procurement departments.

The firm provides end-to-end custom circuit board production solutions, including schematic capture, PCB layout, fabrication management with U.S.-based partners, full turn-key assembly (both manual and automated), cable and wire harness assembly, electro-mechanical enclosure integration, and comprehensive supply chain management with BOM audit, counterfeit detection, and kit verification. MPC imposes no minimum or maximum quantity on fabricated boards, supporting both rapid prototyping and high-volume runs.

MPC serves the electronics industry with a focus on commercial automatic test equipment (ATE), industrial applications, and military high-reliability Class 3 programs.

The company differentiates itself as the only design-to-production firm in the greater Southwest, offering firm fixed pricing, ITAR registration with vetted domestic suppliers, ISO 9001 certification, and adherence to NIST 800-171 data security requirements. Its founding principle—“If you can’t join ’em, beat ’em”—reflects a commitment to comprehensive service and customer-driven flexibility.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR registered','ISO 9001','IPC-A-610 Class I/II/III','J-STD-001 Class I/II/III','Pro-STD-001','NIST 800-171']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Schematic capture", "PCB design and layout", "Quick-turn prototyping", "PWB fabrication management", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Full turn-key PCB assembly", "Manual assembly", "Automated assembly", "Cable, wire and harness assembly", "Electro-mechanical enclosure integration", "Supply chain management", "Full turn-key parts procurement", "Consignment inventory management", "Materials management", "BOM audit", "Counterfeit detection and prevention", "Kit verification", "IPC-A-610 Class I/II/III workmanship compliance", "J-STD-001 Class I/II/III soldering compliance", "ISO 9001 quality management", "ITAR compliance", "NIST 800-171 data security compliance", "Hardware engineering support", "Design for manufacturability"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Automatic test equipment (ATE)", "Military high reliability (Class 3)", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high volume, no minimum or maximum quantity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Albuquerque, NM -> db", "Founder started company in early 1990s after being passed for promotion -> /about-us", "Services: schematic capture, PCB layout, fabrication management, turn-key assembly, cable/harness, electro-mechanical enclosures, supply chain management -> /services, /about-us", "No minimum or maximum PWB quantity -> /services", "Assembly team recertified biannually to IPC J-sta