UPDATE companies SET description='Magna Powertrain operates as a dedicated powertrain group within Magna International, headquartered in Troy, Michigan, with significant operations in Muncie, Indiana. The division is led by President Diba Ilunga and functions as a long‑standing supplier to the global automotive industry.

The group designs, develops, tests, and manufactures a full spectrum of powertrain solutions: battery‑electric (BEV) drive units, hybrid systems ranging from 48‑volt mild hybrids to full HEV and PHEV architectures, and conventional modules such as transmissions, all‑wheel‑drive and four‑wheel‑drive units, disconnect systems, and internal‑combustion engine components. Magna Powertrain also produces mechanical components for eDrive systems and integrates hardware with vehicle‑level software. Production spans multiple global sites, including EMAS‑certified facilities that run on 100 % renewable electricity in Europe, and the group reports 97 % recyclability for its transmissions.

Customers are primarily global automotive OEMs seeking high‑volume, precision‑engineered propulsion hardware. A notable strategic partnership is the LG Magna e‑Powertrain joint venture with LG Electronics, aimed at accelerating growth in the electric‑powertrain market. The group serves passenger‑car and light‑commercial‑vehicle platforms across all major regions.

Magna Powertrain positions itself as the preferred source for eDrive mechanical components when precision, experience, and high volumes are required. Its differentiators include a broad electrification portfolio, the LG Magna joint venture, and a sustainability program that targets net‑zero operations, 100 % green electricity at European sites by 2025, and circular‑economy initiatives such as advanced recyclability and remanufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','ISO14001','IATF16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["BEV powertrain design and manufacturing", "Hybrid powertrain design and manufacturing (48V mild hybrid, HEV, PHEV)", "Transmission manufacturing", "AWD/4WD systems", "Disconnect systems", "ICE modules and components", "eDrive system mechanical components", "Powertrain testing and validation", "Software integration for software-based vehicles", "Sustainable manufacturing (renewable energy, recyclability)"], "industries": ["Automotive OEMs", "Passenger cars", "Light commercial vehicles", "Electric vehicles (EV)", "Hybrid vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Preferred global manufacturer of mechanical components for eDrive systems", "Strategic joint venture with LG Electronics (LG Magna) for e\u2011mobility", "100\u202f% renewable electricity across European operations (2025 target)", "97\u202f% recyclability of transmissions", "Net\u2011zero roadmaps finalized at EMAS\u2011certified sites"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Troy, MI -> page:/", "Operations in Muncie, IN -> db", "President Diba Ilunga -> page:/", "Subsidiary of Magna International -> page:/", "BEV, hybrid, modules/components, transmissions, AWD/4WD, disconnect systems, ICE components -> page:/", "LG Magna joint venture with LG Electronics -> page:/", "One of world''s largest suppliers of powertrain solutions -> page:/", "100% renewable electricity at European EMAS sites -> page:/", "97% recyclability of transmissions -> page:/", "Net-zero roadmaps across EMAS sites -> page:/", "Certifications: ISO9001, ISO14001, IATF16949 -> db", "Preferred global manufacturer of mechanical components for eDrive systems -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Magna is the preferred global manufacturer of mechanical components for eDrive systems when precision, experience, and high volumes are required.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='magna-powertrain' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Magna-Power Electronics has operated from Flemington, New Jersey since its founding in 1981. The company designs and manufactures programmable DC power supplies and electronic loads at its vertically integrated headquarters, where engineering and production share the same campus.

The product line spans more than 250,000 configurations, with DC power supplies ranging from 1.5 kW to over 10,000 kW and electronic loads from 1.25 kW to 20 kW+. In-house capabilities include sheet-metal fabrication, CNC vertical and horizontal machining, wire EDM, robotic bonded-fin heat-sink assembly, SMT and through-hole PCB assembly, precision brazing for water-cooled magnetics, powder coating, custom wood packaging, and wire-harness fabrication across 14 assembly stations. The company reports 475+ megawatts shipped and 50,000+ units delivered, with a typical made-to-order build time of four to six weeks.

Customers range from startups to Fortune 500 firms in aerospace (GE Aviation, Lockheed Martin), defense (QinetiQ), academic research (University of Houston, George Washington University, Colorado School of Mines), robotics (Blue Robotics), energy (Alencon Systems), and hypersonic test facilities (UTSI).

Magna-Power attributes its differentiation to vertical integration, which gives complete control over quality, cost, and lead times, and to a unified control platform (MagnaLINK™) that keeps firmware, commands, and I/O consistent across product families. Stocked common assemblies enable the cited four-to-six-week lead times.', certifications=ARRAY['CEMARK']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Programmable DC power supply design and manufacture (1.5 kW \u2013 10,000 kW+)", "DC electronic load design and manufacture (1.25 kW \u2013 20 kW+)", "Sheet-metal fabrication and powder coating (iron phosphate wash, masking, electrostatic spray, bake)", "CNC vertical machining centers (wet/dry)", "CNC horizontal machining for high-voltage insulators", "Wire EDM for intricate parts", "Robotic bonded-fin heat-sink assembly", "SMT assembly with Europlacer stencil printer and IINEO pick-and-place", "Through-hole insertion lines for power components (2 lines)", "Precision brazing and fabrication for water-cooled magnetics and liquid-piping systems", "Custom shunt fabrication for precision current sensing", "Wire harnessing and preparation with internally developed harness boards", "Final assembly across 14 stations", "Custom wood packaging fabrication", "Metal sanding for deburring and powder-coat prep", "External accessories and integration services", "High Slew Rate Output option (+HS)", "Integrated Blocking Diode option (+BD)", "Water Cooling option (+WC)", "DBx Module (ultra-high stability high-performance)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Academic Research", "Robotics", "Energy", "Hypersonics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Europlacer stencil printer", "IINEO pick-and-place machine", "CNC vertical machining centers", "CNC horizontal machining centers", "Wire EDM", "Robotic bonded-fin heat-sink assembly system", "Through-hole insertion lines (2)", "Assembly stations (14)", "Internally developed wire-harness boards"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4-6 weeks for made-t