UPDATE companies SET description='Magnum Electronics, Inc. is a family-owned communications systems integrator headquartered in Dover, Delaware. The company focuses on supporting mission-critical emergency workers in government and enterprise.

The firm supplies and services public-safety digital two-way radio systems, 4G LTE wireless networks, rugged mobile computers, and GPS fleet management solutions. As a Motorola Solutions Elite Channel Partner, Manufacturer Representative, and Service Partner Center, it provides an extensive selection of radio accessories from brands such as David Clark and 3M Peltor. Its certified factory-trained technical staff offers system design for RF, LTE, and WiFi networks, FCC licensing assistance, professional installation and vehicle upfitting, fleet management with AI-powered video telematics, bench-level repair and programming, and flexible radio rentals using nationwide FCC frequencies. The company also holds State of Delaware contracts for equipment and installation services and is an approved vendor for Delaware SB79 in-building public-safety coverage testing.

Magnum serves law enforcement, fire and EMS agencies, government entities, enterprise customers, educational institutions, and businesses. Its solutions address public-safety communications, construction and public-works fleets, and mobile workforce connectivity.

The company differentiates itself through its Cradlepoint partnership for LTE 4G wireless networks, factory-certified repair with serial-number configuration archiving, and membership in the Enterprise Wireless Alliance. Its focus on interoperability and training in LTE network technology aims to bridge the transition from digital RF voice to IP-based wireless networks.', certifications=ARRAY['Motorola Solutions Elite Channel Partner','Motorola Solutions Manufacturer Representative','Motorola Solutions Federal Market MR','Motorola Solutions Service Partner Center','Cradlepoint Premier Partner','Ericsson certified','3M certified','Whelen certified','Federal Signal certified','Delaware SB79 Compliance Testing approved vendor','Enterprise Wireless Alliance member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF system design", "LTE network design", "WiFi system design", "FCC licensing assistance", "Installation and vehicle upfitting", "Fleet management and GPS tracking", "AI video telematics", "Radio repair and programming", "Radio rentals", "P25 public safety radio systems", "MOTOTRBO DMR digital networks", "Wireless intercom systems", "Delaware SB79 compliance testing", "Motorola serial number decoding", "Turnkey project implementation", "Custom wireless architectures", "Emergency warning lighting installation", "Mobile video and rugged computer installation", "LTE router and GPS fleet management installation", "Cabinet and secure storage installation", "Amber safety lighting installation", "Whelen QuickFit drill-free mounting", "Asset and trailer visibility tracking", "Real-time vehicle diagnostics"], "industries": ["Law Enforcement", "Fire & EMS", "Government", "Enterprise", "Education", "Business", "Public Safety", "Construction", "Public Works"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Motorola APX series", "Motorola XTS series", "Motorola CP series", "Kenwood NX series", "Kenwood VP series", "EFJ VP series", "L3Harris XL series", "Cradlepoint routers", "MOTOTRBO DMR systems", 